==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|mal|treat|lang=en}}, after {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|maltraiter}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/malˈtɹiːt/|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[treat]] [[badly]], to [[abuse]]. {{defdate|from 18th c.}}
#* '''1977''', {{w|Alistair Horne}}, ''A Savage War of Peace'', New York Review Books 2006, p. 217:
#*: he received a telegram from the prime minister ordering that on no account were Yacef and Zohra Drif to be '''maltreated''' in any way.

